 and singlet oxygen</article-title><source>Free Radic Biol Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>721</fpage><lpage>730</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7750796</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0891-5849(94)00192-M</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kvam</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tyrrell</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Induction of oxidative DNA base damage in human skin cells by UV and near visible radiation</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>1997</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>2379</fpage><lpage>2384</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9450485</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/carcin/18.12.2379</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Godar</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>UVA1 radiation triggers two different final apoptotic pathways</article-title><source>J Invest Dermatol</source><year>1999</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9886256</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1523-1747.1999.00474.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pourzand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tyrrell</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Apoptosis, the role of oxidative stress and the example of solar UV radiation</article-title><source>Photochem Photobiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>380</fpage><lpage>390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10546543</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1562/0031-8655(1999)070&#x0003c;0380:ATROOS&#x0003e;2.3.CO;2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Setlow</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Grist</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Woodhead</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wavelengths effective in induction of malignant melanoma</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>1993</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>6666</fpage><lpage>6670</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8341684</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.90.14.6666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Runger</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of UVA in the pathogenesis of melanoma and non-melanoma skin cancer. A short review</article-title><source>Photodermatol Photoimmunol Photomed</source><year>1999</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>212</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10599968</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahlback</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Setlow</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiological support for an hypothesis for melanoma induction indicating a role for UVA radiation</article-title><source>Photochem Photobiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>243</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10461463</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1562/0031-8655(1999)070&#x0003c;0243:ESFAHF&#x0003e;2.3.CO;2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pastila</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Leszczynski</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ultraviolet A exposure alters adhesive properties of mouse melanoma cells</article-title><source>Photodermatol Photoimmunol Photomed</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>234</fpage><lpage>241</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16149935</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-0781.2005.00166.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pastila</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Leszczynski</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ultraviolet A exposure might increase metastasis of mouse melanoma: a pilot study</article-title><source>Photodermatol Photoimmunol Photomed</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15998366</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-0781.2005.00156.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Factor</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Thorgeirsson</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of cyclin G1 during murine hepatic regeneration following Dipin-induced DNA damage</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>1998</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>537</fpage><lpage>546</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9696022</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hep.510280235</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shimizu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishida</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ueoka</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kato</surname><giv